WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:07.006
- [Mark] All right, Alex.

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:07.839
- Sir.

00:00:07.839 --> 00:00:08.820
- [Mark] Alex, where'd you grow up?

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.380
Where are you from originally?

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:11.930
- [Alex] Born and raised in Pico Rivera.

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:12.763
- [Mark] Pico Rivera.

00:00:12.763 --> 00:00:14.027
- [Alex] Yeah.

00:00:14.027 --> 00:00:14.860
- [Mark] Suburb of LA.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.050
And tell me about your childhood.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:17.440
You had both your parents
when you were growing up?

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:18.277
- No, growing up, it was my mother

00:00:18.277 --> 00:00:20.990
and my grandmother, my great-grandmother.

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:23.179
Dad is in prison, you know?

00:00:23.179 --> 00:00:24.863
No type of father figures,

00:00:26.049 --> 00:00:27.878
just women, raised by women.

00:00:27.878 --> 00:00:29.723
- [Mark] And how was your childhood?

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:34.037
- It was all right.

00:00:35.112 --> 00:00:36.560
I don't have too many bad memories of it.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:40.330
But now that I'm older
and look back at it,

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:41.780
it lacked a lot of affection.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.920
- [Mark] And you joined
the gang at what age?

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.410
- About 14, I became a full-blown member.

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:48.243
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:00:50.866 --> 00:00:52.552
And you've done prison
time, I assume, right?

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:53.840
- Yes, sir.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:55.260
- [Mark] When did that start for you?

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:56.560
- Well, I started doing juvenile hall

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:58.580
at 13, 14 years old, you know what I mean?

00:00:58.580 --> 00:00:59.842
And you know, when I was 17,

00:00:59.842 --> 00:01:02.690
I was around my older homeboys.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:05.380
Older than me, dudes were like
25, 26 years old, you know?

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:06.997
And I started doing armed
robberies with them.

00:01:06.997 --> 00:01:09.304
And we started doing real heavier crimes,

00:01:09.304 --> 00:01:11.180
I was doing heavier
crimes with older dudes.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:13.850
So I was imprisoned at 18.

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:14.683
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:19.440
So that means YA, at that point?

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:20.440
- No, state prison.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:21.326
- Oh, prison?

00:01:21.326 --> 00:01:22.170
- Yeah, state prison.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.183
At 17 years, eight
months, they convicted me.

00:01:25.076 --> 00:01:26.188
- [Mark] And what was that for?

00:01:26.188 --> 00:01:28.826
- Laying in wait, attempted murder.

00:01:28.826 --> 00:01:29.659
- [Mark] Attempted murder, it's the same--

00:01:29.659 --> 00:01:31.107
- And laying in wait.

00:01:31.107 --> 00:01:32.380
Parked in front of his house,

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:35.040
waiting for anybody to come
in and out of the house

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.470
to jump out and get him.

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:37.820
- [Mark] Okay.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:39.090
So how many years did you do?

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:40.820
- I did 16 years, eight months.

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:42.440
- [Mark] 16 years.

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:44.160
So, I mean, prison,

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:46.350
you were in and out, I assume?

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:47.813
- I did my 16 years straight.

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:50.790
Got out, stood out for a good three years.

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:52.960
It's easier if you stood out.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:54.480
And then I started fucking around

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:55.700
in my neighborhood again,

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:56.819
started hanging out with
my neighborhood gang

00:01:56.819 --> 00:01:57.820
and started just, you know.

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:02.730
I started violating and just
spiraled back down again.

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:05.260
Now I'm back running
around the streets again.

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:07.210
- [Mark] You've been
out for how many years?

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:08.043
- Since 2014.

00:02:09.794 --> 00:02:12.660
- [Mark] And did that
lifestyle affect your,

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:13.493
like, do you have family?

00:02:13.493 --> 00:02:14.460
Do you have kids, do you have a wife?

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:16.223
- Well, I didn't have my family

00:02:16.223 --> 00:02:17.520
until after I got out of prison.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:21.040
But yeah, now it's affecting it.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.040
It has affected my relationship

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:23.960
with my wife and my kids right here.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:25.120
- [Mark] Yeah, did you raise your kids?

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:27.100
Were you there for them?

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:28.583
- All through the pregnancies,
for my son and my daughter,

00:02:28.583 --> 00:02:29.960
I was at the whole pregnancies.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:31.170
I was there till my daughter was four

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:32.420
and my son was three.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:35.060
Well, going on three,
that's when we broke up.

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:35.893
- [Mark] Okay.

00:02:35.893 --> 00:02:37.060
- Yeah.

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:38.800
- [Mark] And looking back at your life,

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.300
do you have regrets of this?

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:42.617
- Oh yeah, I have regrets, but same time,

00:02:42.617 --> 00:02:44.780
I'm like, "Fuck it, I did
it, I chose this lifestyle."

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:45.613
You know what I mean?

00:02:45.613 --> 00:02:49.567
So I'm doing it, what more
can I say other than that?

00:02:49.567 --> 00:02:50.990
- [Mark] You're still doing it?

00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:52.260
- I run around still, yeah.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:53.093
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:56.490
So did drugs come into the picture

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:57.590
for you at some point?

00:02:58.680 --> 00:02:59.980
- In prison, you know.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:02.613
Prior to prison, I wasn't
too heavy into drugs.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:05.456
But in prison, I didn't have much to do,

00:03:05.456 --> 00:03:06.289
you know what I mean?

00:03:06.289 --> 00:03:07.520
You're sitting in a cell.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.207
I did all my time with a little 401 80.

00:03:09.207 --> 00:03:10.040
You know what I mean,
they've gotta be lasting

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:10.923
or you're slammed down.

00:03:12.831 --> 00:03:13.993
It's one of the only things to do,

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:16.170
one of the escapes, I guess you'd say.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:17.003
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:03:17.003 --> 00:03:18.840
And was there heroin?

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:19.673
- Heroin.

00:03:19.673 --> 00:03:21.830
- [Mark] Yeah, that seems to
be the go-to drug for the--

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:23.017
- Well, it knocks you out,
puts you out for the day.

00:03:23.017 --> 00:03:25.873
Kills the whole day, kills time, you know?

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:30.528
- [Mark] So what kind
of stories can you tell?

00:03:30.528 --> 00:03:32.268
- Aw man, I don't know, man.
(Mark laughs)

00:03:32.268 --> 00:03:33.101
- [Mark] I'm sure you got

00:03:33.101 --> 00:03:35.780
more than a few.
(Alex laughs)

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:39.090
- Like, foul ones, there are
some that are just like...

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:39.973
It depends what you--

00:03:39.973 --> 00:03:42.654
- [Mark] Give me the most
horrifying story you got.

00:03:42.654 --> 00:03:45.173
You can be vague about some
details if you need to.

00:03:45.173 --> 00:03:47.590
To protect the guilty.
- Yeah.

00:03:48.874 --> 00:03:49.707
All right.

00:03:49.707 --> 00:03:51.007
2000, I was a porter.

00:03:51.007 --> 00:03:53.750
You know, a janitor in the buildings.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:55.131
And we were waiting for somebody

00:03:55.131 --> 00:03:56.181
to come back from a visit.

00:03:56.181 --> 00:03:57.400
And he's bringing in dope, you know,

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:58.799
everybody's waiting for him to get back.

00:03:58.799 --> 00:04:00.999
Well, my door stays cracked open

00:04:00.999 --> 00:04:02.710
'cause I go in and out, I'm a porter.

00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:04.270
So when the dude comes
back from the visit,

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:05.260
I go straight over there and I'm like,

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:06.093
"'Ey, come on."

00:04:06.093 --> 00:04:07.267
And he's like, "Well hold
on, let me do my thing first.

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:08.100
"Come back in a half hour or so."

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.040
And I was like, man.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:11.190
I come back in a half hour and he's dead.

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:12.750
He's OD'ed, you know what I mean?

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:13.700
And I'm like damn, I
don't know what to do.

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:15.240
So I go call someone who's waiting

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:16.073
for another guy, right?

00:04:16.073 --> 00:04:17.517
I say "Hey man, come here.

00:04:17.517 --> 00:04:18.520
"What do we do?"

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:20.100
And he was like, "Fuck, how
long has he been like this?"

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:20.933
I said, "I don't know, he told me

00:04:20.933 --> 00:04:22.054
"to come back in a half hour
and I came back in a half hour

00:04:22.054 --> 00:04:23.227
"and this is how I found him."

00:04:23.227 --> 00:04:24.510
And he said, "Well, where's the dope at?"

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:26.240
I said, "I don't know
where the dope's at."

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:27.394
And he was like, "What do
you mean you don't know?"

00:04:27.394 --> 00:04:28.703
I go like, "I don't know
where the fucking dope's at.

00:04:28.703 --> 00:04:30.210
"I don't know, he didn't have no dope."

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:31.570
So we looked around real quick for dope,

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:32.620
we couldn't find none.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:34.340
So this dude, older dude, about 50,

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:37.110
snaps his fingers and goes,
"Fuck, it's still inside him."

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:39.800
And I was like, "All right, well, okay."

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:41.352
He was like, "Get some gloves."

00:04:41.352 --> 00:04:42.670
And I was like "Get some gloves?"

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:44.270
He's like "Yeah, get some gloves."

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:46.257
So first you get gloves,
and then he's like,

00:04:46.257 --> 00:04:48.010
"Go bring some razors."

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.828
I'm like, "What do you do?"

00:04:49.828 --> 00:04:51.060
He's like, "We gotta get
that out of his ass."

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:52.449
And I was like, "What do you
mean get it out of his ass?"

00:04:52.449 --> 00:04:53.347
He was like, "We're gonna cut his ass open

00:04:53.347 --> 00:04:54.180
"and I'm gonna put a fucking glove on,

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:56.920
"and I'ma get the dope out of his ass."

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:58.640
So that's what we did.

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:00.290
And that was pretty fucking foul.

00:05:03.487 --> 00:05:05.046
It was an experience, I mean.

00:05:05.046 --> 00:05:06.740
It's for dope.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.070
It's just to get that stupid dope.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:08.930
We got in trouble behind it

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:10.413
at the end of the day, anyway.

00:05:11.294 --> 00:05:12.127
You know?

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:18.680
That was my bad memories
in prison, you know?

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:20.230
It wasn't good, it--

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:21.200
- [Mark] That was in prison?

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.320
- That was in prison, yeah.

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:23.153
And that's--

00:05:23.153 --> 00:05:24.340
- [Mark] Is the gang life in prison,

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:26.320
I know it's different,
but how is it different

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:29.113
than outside on the street?

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:32.373
- Your homeboys on the streets,

00:05:32.373 --> 00:05:33.900
you're not only homeboys, you're friends.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:34.970
A lot of them, you went
to school with them,

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:35.803
you have friendships with them,

00:05:35.803 --> 00:05:37.840
you know their families
and things like this.

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:38.970
So there's a lot more leniency

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:40.320
amongst each other, you know?

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:42.070
But in prison, there's no leniency.

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:45.060
When you get there, they
give you the verbal,

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:47.831
here's your verbal, the
rules and regulations.

00:05:47.831 --> 00:05:48.710
And they give you something to read

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:49.610
that has all the rules.

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:51.040
And those are your two warning shots,

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:52.632
anything after this, no more,
we're not talking to you.

00:05:52.632 --> 00:05:56.150
Right now it's just, we're gonna do you.

00:05:56.150 --> 00:05:57.707
Back at that time when I was in prison,

00:05:57.707 --> 00:05:58.610
there was that race riot.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:00.370
There were racial issues, you know?

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:01.460
Right now, it's not so bad

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:03.140
with the racial issues back to how it was

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:05.463
in Calapat, in Ironwood, places like that.

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:08.300
You only had one opportunity to mess up,

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:09.730
you messed up, you're out of here.

00:06:09.730 --> 00:06:12.780
We can't afford to have
no fuck-ups, none of that.

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:14.820
Everybody has to be
ready to go at all times.

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:17.040
Everybody has to be thinking all the time.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:18.397
You can't be like, "Oh, I just woke up

00:06:18.397 --> 00:06:19.410
"and I wasn't thinking."

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:21.541
There's none of that, you know?

00:06:21.541 --> 00:06:22.750
So less lenient, you know what I mean?

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:23.636
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:06:23.636 --> 00:06:24.790
Were you around for the drive-by era,

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:25.950
or not really?
- Yeah.

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:27.040
Heavily, yeah.

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:29.810
- [Mark] So drive-bys were
for what purpose, just--

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:31.920
- [Alex] Just to shoot somebody.

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:33.803
Shoot someone, you know?

00:06:34.844 --> 00:06:36.670
Back then in the drive-by zone,

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:39.295
I don't know if it was because

00:06:39.295 --> 00:06:40.490
there were more guns
in the streets or what.

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:41.930
I don't know the reason why.

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:44.230
But back then, everybody shot back.

00:06:44.230 --> 00:06:46.342
Now you can shoot at
somebody and half the time,

00:06:46.342 --> 00:06:47.500
they don't even really shoot back at you.

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:48.840
But back in the drive-by times,

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:50.190
when you came by and you shot at somebody,

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:52.270
it's 'cause everybody would
shoot right back at you,

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:53.103
you know what I mean?

00:06:53.103 --> 00:06:53.936
Most of the time.

00:06:53.936 --> 00:06:56.090
So it wasn't like you're
just driving guns.

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:57.871
Like, driving in front of the center,

00:06:57.871 --> 00:06:59.470
you're just stopping
and shooting somebody.

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:00.990
You expected for them to shoot back,

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:02.970
or like they might have homeboys
on the side of the street

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:04.651
or something, you know what I mean?

00:07:04.651 --> 00:07:05.951
It was a lot more gunplay.

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:10.407
When I was growing up in the early '90s,

00:07:10.407 --> 00:07:11.520
the late '80s, early '90s,

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:13.090
especially in the
Southeast, South Hollywood,

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:14.290
Beachwood and Whittier,
Norwalk and all that?

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:16.650
There was a lot of gang mines.

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:18.820
It was like all day, every day.

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:20.720
It wasn't like at the middle of the night.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:22.590
It was like, "Let's go right
now when school gets out."

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:26.700
'Cause there's just trains,
airplanes, there's traffic,

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:28.292
no one's gonna hear the
gunshots two, three blocks away

00:07:28.292 --> 00:07:30.410
like they would at night, you know?

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:31.463
So that was in my teens.

00:07:31.463 --> 00:07:32.870
After school, we'd go over
to my enemy's neighborhood,

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:35.690
to the high schools in their neighborhood.

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:37.910
And they'd be hanging
out with their bitches,

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:38.743
we'd go over there, look for them,

00:07:38.743 --> 00:07:40.261
and try to shoot them.

00:07:40.261 --> 00:07:41.094
Plain and simple, you know?

00:07:41.094 --> 00:07:44.190
- [Mark] As an outsider
looking at the gang world,

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:45.420
it just seems ridiculous to me

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:46.850
that there can be somebody

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:48.910
who lives in the town next to you

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:51.400
who's your enemy for no good reason

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:54.830
other than just he lives
across the tracks from you.

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:55.838
- Well, the thing is--

00:07:55.838 --> 00:07:57.740
- And you could be friends with him today.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:07:58.733
- You're right.

00:07:58.733 --> 00:08:00.750
It doesn't make sense,

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:02.818
but if everything did make sense.

00:08:02.818 --> 00:08:06.020
And other people don't
understand on the outside,

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:07.497
they say, "How can you
fight for the street

00:08:07.497 --> 00:08:08.391
"or fight for these,"

00:08:08.391 --> 00:08:09.224
You're not fighting for that,

00:08:09.224 --> 00:08:10.057
they're fighting for a blood feud.

00:08:10.057 --> 00:08:11.940
They already exist because maybe

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:12.990
while you were in junior high,

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:14.970
they killed your friend, fucking Michael,

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:16.160
who was from the gang.

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:18.030
Before you though, you know, maybe.

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:19.340
So now you've already lost friends

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:20.350
to this blood feud that's going on.

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:22.510
And it's not even about
this or that anyone,

00:08:22.510 --> 00:08:23.430
it's about they're killing us,

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:24.321
we gotta go kill them now.

00:08:24.321 --> 00:08:26.459
That's what's happening, you know?

00:08:26.459 --> 00:08:29.466
- [Mark] It's almost like
human nature on some level.

00:08:29.466 --> 00:08:30.330
- Yeah, gangs are like tribes.

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:32.950
It's like tribal warfare,
you know what I mean?

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:33.924
Pretty much, you know?

00:08:33.924 --> 00:08:35.091
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:08:36.237 --> 00:08:37.890
And your kids are following

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:38.950
in your dad's footsteps, or no?

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:39.880
- No, hell no.

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:40.970
Not at all.

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:43.483
My babies' mama, she was born
and raised in Catalina Island.

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:47.150
They're white people,
you know what I mean?

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:48.497
I don't mean that disrespectfully,

00:08:48.497 --> 00:08:49.828
but they're square people,
you know what I mean?

00:08:49.828 --> 00:08:50.661
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:08:50.661 --> 00:08:51.494
- They worked all their life.

00:08:51.494 --> 00:08:53.930
They're not being raised in
a bad environment at all.

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:55.830
- [Mark] What do they think of their dad?

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:57.537
- They love me, my kids love me.

00:08:57.537 --> 00:08:58.877
They don't see nothing other but me.

00:08:58.877 --> 00:09:01.030
They just know me, getting
up and getting them bottles,

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:02.880
getting up and watching PBS with them,

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:03.763
or getting up and putting
a movie on for them.

00:09:03.763 --> 00:09:04.900
That's all they know.

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:06.640
- [Mark] But you have a
good relationship with them?

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:07.473
- Yeah.

00:09:07.473 --> 00:09:08.306
- [Mark] With your kids?

00:09:08.306 --> 00:09:09.139
- Yeah, yeah.

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:13.550
Her name is Grace, since
me and Grace have broke up,

00:09:15.002 --> 00:09:16.130
she uses them a little more

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:18.665
as sort of tools to her a little more.

00:09:18.665 --> 00:09:19.842
'Cause I could care
less about her no more,

00:09:19.842 --> 00:09:20.791
but sometimes she likes to use the kids

00:09:20.791 --> 00:09:22.791
as a way to, you know...

00:09:24.844 --> 00:09:26.021
Well, what can you do, you know?

00:09:26.021 --> 00:09:26.950
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:31.311
How has the gang experienced
change since you were young?

00:09:31.311 --> 00:09:32.685
- Oh, it's weak now.

00:09:32.685 --> 00:09:34.852
It's not the same no more.

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:37.013
I remember when I was younger,

00:09:37.013 --> 00:09:39.023
the older guys used to say that about us.

00:09:40.286 --> 00:09:41.860
And now I know it's not just
something that's being said,

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:42.867
'cause you look back and you're like,

00:09:42.867 --> 00:09:44.657
"Man, back then we would've done this,

00:09:44.657 --> 00:09:45.490
"or we would've done that."

00:09:45.490 --> 00:09:47.307
Or "Back then, those guys couldn't have

00:09:47.307 --> 00:09:48.140
"come into our neighborhood

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:50.190
"right on the wall back then."

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:51.812
It's things like that, you know?

00:09:51.812 --> 00:09:53.264
You knew the difference, you know?

00:09:53.264 --> 00:09:54.097
- [Mark] There was more loyalty?

00:09:54.097 --> 00:09:55.732
- A lot more loyalty.

00:09:55.732 --> 00:09:56.700
And you know, it's funny,

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:57.970
I tell this to people, like
people don't understand it.

00:09:57.970 --> 00:10:02.090
But I blame the attitude
on fucking rap music,

00:10:02.090 --> 00:10:03.757
like Black music, those that are like,

00:10:03.757 --> 00:10:04.590
"Fuck everybody, I'm just trying

00:10:04.590 --> 00:10:05.460
"to get money for myself."

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:06.470
And they're all individualists.

00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:08.560
Coming into a gang and
being all by yourself,

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:10.663
that's not game mentality,
you know what I mean?

00:10:10.663 --> 00:10:12.240
That game mentality's lacking now,

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:13.232
like one for everybody.

00:10:13.232 --> 00:10:14.117
Everybody's kind of like,

00:10:14.117 --> 00:10:18.227
"Why join a group if you wanna be alone?"

00:10:19.710 --> 00:10:22.090
So lacks a lot of loyalty.

00:10:22.090 --> 00:10:23.180
- [Mark] What's the most important lesson

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:24.920
you've learned in life?

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:30.310
- Don't tell nobody what you're doing.

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:31.143
Ever.

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:34.710
Or where you're going, just don't.

00:10:34.710 --> 00:10:36.660
You just don't tell
nobody nothing, you know?

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:37.660
Pretty much.

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:40.790
That's the best way to say it, yeah.

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:44.240
- [Mark] Where do you see
your life going from here?

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:45.460
How old are you?

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:46.293
- I'm 43.

00:10:46.293 --> 00:10:47.530
- [Mark] 43?

00:10:47.530 --> 00:10:48.363
Still young.

00:10:48.363 --> 00:10:49.196
- Yeah.

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:52.063
It's hard, man.

00:10:52.063 --> 00:10:54.900
Because I've been doing
jail or prison all my life.

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:55.953
And my dad it, and my grandpa did it.

00:10:55.953 --> 00:10:57.843
I mean, my dad is still
in prison right now.

00:10:57.843 --> 00:11:00.190
He's 67 years old, he's still in prison.

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:02.850
And my uncle's sort of like that.

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:03.683
I look at them, I'm like,

00:11:03.683 --> 00:11:05.587
"Fuck, man, I don't
want to be 55 years old,

00:11:05.587 --> 00:11:07.010
"still going and doing violations."

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:08.273
I'm 43 and I keep doin' 'em,

00:11:08.273 --> 00:11:09.106
why are you going there?

00:11:09.106 --> 00:11:10.210
Now I'm already like,
"I can't do this shit."

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:11.703
These people around me get nervous.

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:13.433
You know what I'm saying?

00:11:13.433 --> 00:11:14.629
- [Mark] But with your record,

00:11:14.629 --> 00:11:15.580
it's going to be hard to
get a square job, right?

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:17.270
- Yeah, it's hard.

00:11:17.270 --> 00:11:21.130
But I don't even worry
about trying to have a job.

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:22.300
Honestly, I don't worry about that

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:23.670
because I'm trying to get money

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:25.320
however I can and wherever I can.

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:29.550
And unfortunately, that's the
situation I put myself in.

00:11:29.550 --> 00:11:31.760
So I accept it for what it is, you know?

00:11:31.760 --> 00:11:33.080
At the same time, though,

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:35.160
if I were to put my habits aside,

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:37.600
and I go to a job agency,
they'll give me a fucking job

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:38.570
and I can go work, you know what I mean?

00:11:38.570 --> 00:11:40.570
It's not impossible for me to get a job.

00:11:43.594 --> 00:11:45.451
To me, that's making excuses, lying,

00:11:45.451 --> 00:11:47.277
for not really wanting to work.

00:11:47.277 --> 00:11:49.840
'Cause you can get a job.

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:52.216
- [Mark] You think the gang direction

00:11:52.216 --> 00:11:55.034
for young men is more a
product of environment

00:11:55.034 --> 00:11:58.083
or the family, or the friends he had?

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:01.030
What do you think got you into the gang?

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:03.800
Or gets young men to follow that path?

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:05.570
'Cause if you grow up in
Santa Barbara or something,

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:06.522
you probably wouldn't--

00:12:06.522 --> 00:12:07.355
- Yeah, and you got gang members

00:12:07.355 --> 00:12:08.188
coming out of Santa Barbara.

00:12:08.188 --> 00:12:09.200
I don't understand that.

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:11.717
I think it's the environment a little bit,

00:12:11.717 --> 00:12:13.590
but at the same time, it's also...

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:23.303
A lack of belonging somewhere.

00:12:25.705 --> 00:12:28.093
Life is social, you gotta be
put in some type of group,

00:12:29.379 --> 00:12:30.212
you gotta be accepted

00:12:30.212 --> 00:12:31.283
by whoever you're gonna be accepted by.

00:12:31.283 --> 00:12:32.410
Because everybody wants to be accepted

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:33.243
by somebody or whatever.

00:12:33.243 --> 00:12:34.076
- [Mark] That becomes your family?

00:12:34.076 --> 00:12:35.800
- Yeah, you know what I mean?

00:12:37.780 --> 00:12:40.373
And maybe gangs, they look good to people.

00:12:40.373 --> 00:12:41.610
Basically, it looks good,

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:42.992
you get girls or whatever the fuck,

00:12:42.992 --> 00:12:44.140
you're doing this, you're doing that.

00:12:44.140 --> 00:12:46.440
But you don't see the other side

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:47.733
before you join a gang

00:12:47.733 --> 00:12:49.450
that you're going to prison.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:50.600
You're from a gang,
you're going to prison.

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:51.940
And now there's people,
there's gang members

00:12:51.940 --> 00:12:52.883
who are like hoping to dodge prison.

00:12:52.883 --> 00:12:55.420
It's like, that's part of the lifestyle.

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:56.960
Prison's gonna happen,
you know what I mean?

00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:59.060
Just for how long is the question.

00:12:59.060 --> 00:13:01.860
But if you're a gang member,
you're going to prison.

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:02.970
Otherwise you're not being a gang member.

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:04.717
I don't know what you're doing,

00:13:04.717 --> 00:13:06.540
but you're not being a gang member.

00:13:06.540 --> 00:13:07.373
- [Mark] What advice would you give

00:13:07.373 --> 00:13:09.450
to a young man who's
considering doing this?

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:11.618
Today?

00:13:11.618 --> 00:13:14.035
(Alex sighs)

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:20.520
- I'm not gonna say it's
not worth it nowadays,

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:22.509
'cause everybody's worth it.

00:13:22.509 --> 00:13:23.910
To other people, even to me.

00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:27.980
I have no regrets about it.

00:13:27.980 --> 00:13:30.417
But I would just say,

00:13:30.417 --> 00:13:32.410
"Make sure it's really what you wanna do."

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:33.810
'Cause you gotta carry that
around with you forever,

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:34.985
you know what I mean?

00:13:34.985 --> 00:13:38.570
And some people aren't
capable of the violence,

00:13:38.570 --> 00:13:39.403
they think they are.

00:13:39.403 --> 00:13:40.660
And so they do it,

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:41.820
and then they gotta keep to themselves.

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:45.277
I've seen some people not be
able to handle the violence,

00:13:45.277 --> 00:13:46.110
and they do.

00:13:50.170 --> 00:13:51.080
Everybody thinks they can
do this, they can do that,

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:52.810
but when they actually have
to get up there and do it,

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:54.510
and you do it, how are
you gonna feel afterwards?

00:13:54.510 --> 00:13:55.343
- [Mark] And you live with it

00:13:55.343 --> 00:13:56.176
for the rest of your life.

00:13:56.176 --> 00:13:57.009
- Yeah, are you gonna be able

00:13:57.009 --> 00:13:59.150
to sleep with yourself
after that, you know?

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:03.853
So it's like, make sure
you're really ready to do,

00:14:05.310 --> 00:14:07.920
ready to take that step, you know?

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:09.180
And to be able to control it.

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:11.850
Once you do take that step,

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:13.140
now it's a question of like,

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:15.250
having to decide when to do that.

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:17.510
Now it's not an issue like

00:14:17.510 --> 00:14:19.070
being boastful or prideful when I say,

00:14:19.070 --> 00:14:19.930
I already know I could do that.

00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:21.830
But can I do it and get away with it?

00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:24.959
And if I do do it, what's
gonna happen afterwards?

00:14:24.959 --> 00:14:25.792
You know, now it's a question of that.

00:14:25.792 --> 00:14:26.760
It's not about...

00:14:28.820 --> 00:14:29.804
- [Mark] Pulling the trigger.

00:14:29.804 --> 00:14:32.098
- Yeah, it's not just
pulling the trigger no more.

00:14:32.098 --> 00:14:34.948
Now there's other things you
gotta contemplate, you know?

00:14:36.677 --> 00:14:37.510
- [Mark] All right, Alex.

00:14:37.510 --> 00:14:39.150
Well, thank you so much
for talking with me.

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:41.346
And good luck with wherever
you go from here, man.

00:14:41.346 --> 00:14:42.365
- Thank you very much, man.

00:14:42.365 --> 00:14:44.115
- [Mark] Thanks, man.

00:14:48.826 --> 00:14:49.909
That's great.

